## Context

Both peer reviewers (ChatGPT and Claude) flag the reference dataset as a
methodological contribution that must be described in the paper, not assumed.
The gold standard's credibility bounds all three experiments' claims.

`data/reference/vietnam_thermal_v1.csv` exists (163 plants) but its construction
is not described in the manuscript.

## Actions

1. Add a paragraph to `slides/manuscript/main.md` §2 ("The quality bar") or
   as a subsection of Annex A describing:
   - Which primary sources were consulted (PDP7, PDP7A, PDP8 annexes, EVN annual
     reports, MOIT decisions — cross-check against actual data/rag_corpus contents)
   - How conflicts between sources were resolved (which source wins, by what rule)
   - Residual uncertainty: which fields have the most disputed values
     (the 62 "proposed" + 21 "planned" rows carry high uncertainty)
   - Version lock: commit hash or date at which the reference is frozen for
     Experiments 1–3

2. Add a `PROVENANCE.md` in `data/reference/` documenting the above for
   reproducibility.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Provenance paragraph added to the manuscript
- [ ] `data/reference/PROVENANCE.md` written
- [ ] At least the top-3 disputed status cases documented
